By Fermat’s theorem, \(17^{100}\equiv1\pmod{101}\), so
\[
17^{460}\equiv17^{60}\pmod{101}.
\]
Using repeated squaring gives
\[
17^{60}=17^{32+16+8+4}\equiv87\cdot84\cdot36\cdot95\equiv1\pmod{101}.
\]
